---
title: Spiced Biscotti
course: Dessert
tags: 
- Cookies
- Vegan
source: Modified from The Cookie Book
cuisine: American
servings: 35
---

Preheat an oven to 325. Line a #baking sheet{} with parchment paper.

Use an #electric mixer{} on medium speed to beat the @sugar{200%g} and @plant-based milk{120%g} until frothy, about ~{2%minutes}. Use a large metal spoon to fold in @all-purpose flour{370%g}, @baking powder{1%tsp}, @baking soda{1%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{1/2%tsp}, @ground nutmeg{1/2%tsp}, @ground cloves{1/2%tsp}, and @salt{1/4%tsp}. Fold in the @aniseed liqueur{1.5%tsp} and @slivered almonds{140%g}. Mix to a soft dough. 

Divide the dough in half. Briefly knead each portion on a lightly floured surface until smooth. Form each portion into a log 8 x 1.5 inches (20 x 4 cm) thick. Place logs on prepared baking sheet, 4 inches (10 cm) apart. Bake for 45 minutes. Remove from the oven and allow to cool for 5 minutes. 

Using a #serrated knife{}, cut each log into 1/2-inch (12-mm) slices, slightly on the diagonal. Return the slices to the baking tray. You will need to bake in batches. Bake for a further 15 minutes, turning the slices after about ~{7%minutes}, until crisp and lightly golden. Transfer to a wire rack to cool and crisp further. 